      "value": "@{5f2e0a4e8464150716ffd322|full_name}: We tweaked our layout code to be a little more precise, but now it can be a little less forgiving of rogue geometry/parts.\n\nFor avtr_90ac8cf5-8262-4465-ab6c-9dcf1c8b9977, the part that appears to be pushing out the avatar's bounds is the rifle. The mesh itself does seem to have wider bounds than you'd expect. Maybe some hidden geometry?\n\nOn avtr_9030c11b-92b2-45f1-b9e9-7a4fefdaac17, it looks like the staff is probably starting out sideways in the prefab, and is driven by constraints rather than animation. Rotating it so that its initial position is better aligned with the wizard's bounds should solve the problem.\n\nLet me know if these tweaks solve your problem!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
