      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2e0a4e8464150716ffd322|full_name}: The UI has been trying to find the avatar's bounds and perform an \"aspect fit\" into that square in the UI for some time now. Recently, we discovered a couple math bugs and made that process more precise. \n\nSo for some avatars, that might immediately feel like a regression because some cases can be less forgiving than before - but the majority of avatars fit better now, the behavior's more consistent, and it should be easier to troubleshoot individual avatars now.\n\nThe general rule now is that if an avatar's preview looks too small, something in the avatar is making its bounds too wide.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
